  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse rapide &#xe0; la crise humanitaire &#x2013; M23 dans la province du Nord-Kivu en R&#xe9;publique d&#xe9;mocratique du Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving health assistance to internally displaced persons and host community members in Kayna, Karisimbi, Nyiragongo, Rwanguba and Rutshuru. This WHO project carries out disease surveillance, active detection of cholera cases, procures essential medical equipment, and establishes cholera treatment units. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 182,000 people, including 56,000 women, 53,000 men, 73,000 children, and including 19,000 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
